# Internationalization review

Follow `AGENTS.md`, especially its `Internationalization Review` section, for every new or modified code path.

- Review user-visible React copy, accessible labels, errors, Rust/Tauri messages, generated or exported documents, rule-pack fields, and dynamic data for both `zh-CN` and `en`.
- Use the existing i18n helpers and paired Chinese/English contract fields. Do not add a one-language user-facing string or assume an unmapped backend string will be translated.
- Keep user-authored manuscript and quoted source content unchanged while localizing its surrounding interface and provenance labels.
- Add or update focused tests for both locales when the change is user-visible, then mention the internationalization review outcome in the completion summary.
- This rule is advisory context for Cursor. Do not add hooks, CI gates, or build blockers unless the user explicitly requests enforcement.
